# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the PTSC sports-day Next.js project following the latest official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` to package.json
- **Package manager**: npm
- **Lock file updated**: package-lock.json

### 2. Configuration
- **Modified file**: `ptsc/src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Changes**:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added component to root layout: `<SpeedInsights />` placed after `<Analytics />` in the body

### Implementation Details

The project is using:
- **Framework**: Next.js 16.3.3 (App Router)
- **Package manager**: npm
- **TypeScript**: Yes (v6.0.3)

Followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js v13.5+ App Router:
- Retrieved latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Used the framework-specific Next.js App Router implementation
- Placed SpeedInsights component in the root layout alongside the existing Analytics component
- Maintained consistency with existing code patterns (Analytics was already configured)

### Verification Steps Completed

✅ **Build**: Successfully compiled with `npm run build`
✅ **Linter**: No errors with `npm run lint`
✅ **TypeScript**: Type checking passed with `npm run typecheck`
✅ **Tests**: 127 of 130 tests passing (3 pre-existing failures unrelated to Speed Insights, related to missing Python dependencies)

### Next Steps

When deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
2. Data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section
3. No additional configuration is required

### Notes

- The SpeedInsights component was placed next to the existing Analytics component in the root layout
- Both components follow the same import pattern from `@vercel/*` packages
- The implementation is minimal and non-intrusive, following Next.js App Router best practices
- Lock files have been properly updated to ensure consistent dependency resolution
